5. PRE-REGISTRATION OF HYPOTHESES AND DECISION RULES (written before any model is compared)   [0.3 min]
====================================================================================================
H1: Recent PM2.5 concentrations are strong predictors of next-hour PM2.5.
H2: Meteorological and pollutant measurements provide additional predictive information beyond historical PM2.5.
H3: PM2.5 has systematic hourly and weekly temporal patterns that can be captured using temporal features.
H4: Rolling statistics of recent PM2.5 provide more stable predictive information than individual lag values.
decision rule: group removal must raise CV-MAE by >= 1 % in >= 4/5 folds AND joint HAC Wald p < 0.05
model selection: primary metric CV-MAE, ties within 1.0 SE, then the data properties of the training design decide (Ridge / Lasso / ElasticNet)

