Target: PM2.5 concentration at t+1 hour
Target unit: ug/m3

================================================
TASK
================================================
Prediction: X(t) -> PM2.5(t+1)
Allowed at hour t: current pollutants and meteorology, calendar of t, PM2.5 up to t (current value, lags, rolling statistics of the shifted series).
Forbidden: PM2.5(t+1) or any later value, future meteorology, centred rolling windows, any statistic fitted on test data.

================================================
SPLIT
================================================
Train: 28,050 hours 2013-03-01 00:00 -> 2016-05-12 17:00 (26,000 usable)
Test:  7,013 hours 2016-05-12 18:00 -> 2017-02-28 22:00 (6,752 usable)

================================================
HYPOTHESES (pre-registered; verdict from training CV + training inference)
================================================
H1: Supported - Recent PM2.5 predicts next-hour PM2.5 (C vs C - PM2.5 history: dMAE +96.96 %, worse in 5/5 folds; joint Wald p < 1e-300); descriptive test check (not used for the verdict): removing the history changes test MAE by +61.4 %
H2: Supported - Environment adds information beyond PM2.5 history (C vs C - environment block: dMAE +1.48 %, worse in 4/5 folds; joint Wald p = 4e-115); descriptive test check: removing the environment changes test MAE by +0.05 % - the small training-CV gain did not replicate on the test period
H3: Partly supported - Hourly/weekly temporal patterns captured by temporal features (C vs C - calendar terms: dMAE +0.49 %, worse in 2/5 folds; joint Wald p = 8.2e-53); descriptive test check: removing the calendar terms changes test MAE by -0.48 %
H4: Not supported - Rolling statistics more stable than individual lags (lag-only (C - rolling) relative to rolling-only (C - lag); negative = lag-only better: dMAE -0.86 %, worse in 0/5 folds; DM on out-of-fold |error| (rolling-only minus lag-only): mean +0.091, p = 1.6e-39); descriptive test check: test MAE lag-only 10.066 vs rolling-only 10.185; fold-to-fold std of CV-MAE rolling-only 1.30 vs lag-only 1.29

================================================
BEST MODEL
================================================
Model: Lasso regression (linear)
Hyperparameters: {"alpha": 0.21544346900318845}
Feature set: C (engineered)
Why: Best mean CV-MAE: Lasso (10.508); 1 SE = 0.577; families within 1 SE: ['OLS', 'Ridge', 'Lasso', 'ElasticNet']. Training-design properties: max VIF 376.7 (PM25_roll_mean_3), 10 features with VIF > 10; 3 correlated groups (|r| >= 0.8); 50.0% of features weak (|Spearman| < 0.1; threshold 50%). Implied family: ElasticNet (correlated groups of predictors AND many weak/redundant predictors -> feature selection that keeps correlated groups together); pre-registered outcome: ElasticNet. AMENDMENT: Ridge, ElasticNet have their CV-optimal penalty on the no-shrinkage edge of the grid (Ridge: {'alpha': 0.001}, 54/54 non-zero; ElasticNet: {'alpha': 9.999999999999999e-05, 'l1_ratio': 0.9}, 54/54 non-zero), i.e. numerically OLS, so they are skipped -> chosen: Lasso ({'alpha': 0.21544346900318845}, 29/54 non-zero).

